# The BFR Pros - environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local dev (gitignored), and set the same keys in Vercel.
#
# IMPORTANT: the /consulting form saves to Supabase WITHOUT any env vars. It uses
# the publishable anon key (committed in src/lib/constants.ts) plus an INSERT-only
# RLS policy on the consulting_leads table, which is the standard, safe pattern
# for a public form (the public can submit; only you, via the Supabase dashboard,
# can read submissions). So everything below is OPTIONAL.

# --- Email notification to Nick (optional; Resend) ---
# If RESEND_API_KEY is unset, submissions still save to Supabase; no email is sent.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# CONSULTING_NOTIFY_FROM must be a Resend-verified sender. Verify thebfrpros.com in
# Resend first (DNS records), then use e.g. consulting@thebfrpros.com. For a quick
# test before verifying a domain, use: BFR Pros <onboarding@resend.dev>
# (Resend's test sender only delivers to the Resend account owner's address.)
CONSULTING_NOTIFY_FROM=BFR Pros <consulting@thebfrpros.com>
CONSULTING_NOTIFY_TO=nick@thebfrpros.com

# --- Optional hardening (only if you want to stop using the public anon key) ---
# If set, the /api/consulting route uses these instead of the committed anon key.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is secret and server-only; never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://brvebfxaexxjghvwyidy.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
